course: dictionary
lesson: 669
title: Many meanings of baking
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Baking can be a verb, a noun or an adjective, and the sentence tells you which meaning to use. Look at the words next to it: «Mia is baking bread in the oven» shows baking is an action, cooking in an oven.
explain: When baking is a noun, it means the bread and cakes that are baked. When it is an adjective, as in «baking hot», it means very hot. Ask yourself: is it an action, a thing, or a describing word? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Baking also appears in science lessons. «Add a splash of vinegar and it turns pink; add a pinch of baking soda and it turns blue-green.» Here baking soda is a fixed phrase, a named powder. The word baking does not mean cooking in this phrase, so do not guess from the first word alone.
fact: Baking means cooking in an oven.
fact: As a noun, baking can mean the bread and cakes that are baked.
fact: As an adjective, «baking hot» means very hot.
fact: «Cakes rise with baking powder or whisked eggs instead.» Baking powder is used to make cakes rise.
fact: Baking soda and baking powder are not the same thing, so check which one a recipe asks for.
exercise: «Mia is baking bread in the oven.» What is baking? | Swimming in a pool | Sleeping in the sun | Drawing a picture | *Cooking in an oven
exercise: «The sun is baking hot today.» What does baking hot mean? | Slightly wet | Very quiet | *Very hot | Very cold
exercise: Ravi says, «The baking smelled lovely.» What does baking mean here? | Sweeping the floor | *The bread and cakes that have been baked | A cold drink | A type of dance
test: Which phrase uses baking to mean a tray for cooking in an oven? | Baking hot | Baking music | Baking soda | *Baking tray
test: Which sentence uses baking as an adjective? | The baking was sold at the fair | Baking is fun to do with friends | *It is baking hot in the desert today | I am baking a loaf now
exam: Which sentence uses baking as a verb? | *Dad is baking cakes for the school fair | The baking sold out before lunch | Baking soda is a white powder | The oven was baking hot
